    "q-93642": {
      "dom_id": "step-q93642",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. If $23\\,|\\,12a$ then $23\\,|\\,a$\n\nII. If $3\\,|\\,12a$ then $3\\,|\\,a$\n\nIII. If $12\\,|\\,3a$ then $12\\,|\\,a$",
      "worked_solution": "For any integers $a$ and $b,$ and any prime $p,$\n\n$p\\,|\\,ab$ $\\,⟹\\,$ $p\\,|\\,a\\,$ or $\\,p\\,|\\,b.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. As $23$ is prime and $23\\,|\\,12a,$ we must have $23\\,|\\,12$ or $23\\,|\\,a.$ Since $12$ is not divisible by $23,$ we obtain that $a$ must be divisible by $23.$\n\n- Statement II is false. As a counterexample, let $a=2.$ Then, $3∣12\\cdot 2$ but $3∤2.$\n\n- Statement III is false. As a counterexample, let $a=4.$ Then, $12∣3\\cdot 4$ but $12∤4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
