    "q-221513": {
      "dom_id": "step-q221513",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "If $p,$ $q,$ and $k$ are primes with $p\\ne q$, and $p\\,|\\,{q}^{4}{k}^{6},$ then{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that for any integers $a,$ $b,$ and $c,$\n\n$c\\,|\\,ab\\,$ and $\\,\\text{gcd}(a,c)=1$ $\\,⟹\\,$ $\\,c\\,|\\,b.$\n\nAlso, given that $p$ and $r$ are primes, we get\n\n${p}^{m}\\,|\\,{r}^{n}$ $\\,⟹\\,$ $p=r,$\n\nwhere $m$ and $n$ are positive integers.\n\nWith that in mind, we proceed as follows:\n\n- Since $p$ and $q$ are different primes, $\\text{gcd}(p,q)=1.$ Since $p\\,|\\,{q}^{4}{k}^{6},$ we must obtain that\n\n$$\np\\,|\\,{k}^{6}.\n$$\n\n- Since $p$ and $k$ are primes and $p\\,|\\,{k}^{6},$ we get\n\n$$\np=k.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
