    "q-221497": {
      "dom_id": "step-q221497",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "If $p$ and $q$ are primes, $\\text{gcd}(k,p)=1$ and ${p}^{3}\\,|\\,k{q}^{4},$ then{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that for any integers $a,$ $b,$ and $c,$\n\n$c\\,|\\,ab\\,$ and $\\,\\text{gcd}(a,c)=1$ $\\,⟹\\,$ $\\,c\\,|\\,b.$\n\nAlso, given that $p$ and $q$ are primes, we get\n\n${p}^{m}\\,|\\,{q}^{n}$ $\\,⟹\\,$ $p=q,$\n\nwhere $m$ and $n$ are positive integers.\n\nWith that in mind, we proceed as follows:\n\n- Since $\\text{gcd}(k,p)=1,$ we also have $\\text{gcd}(k,{p}^{3})=1.$\n\n- Since $\\text{gcd}(k,{p}^{3})=1$ and ${p}^{3}\\,|\\,k{q}^{4},$ we must obtain that\n\n$$\n{p}^{3}\\,|\\,{q}^{4}.\n$$\n\n- Since $p$ and $q$ are primes and ${p}^{3}\\,|\\,{q}^{4},$ we get\n\n$$\np=q.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
