    "q-221512": {
      "dom_id": "step-q221512",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "If $p,$ $q,$ and $w$ are primes with $p\\ne q$, and $p\\,|\\,q{w}^{4},$ then{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that for any integers $a,$ $b,$ and $c,$\n\n$c\\,|\\,ab\\,$ and $\\,\\text{gcd}(a,c)=1$ $\\,⟹\\,$ $\\,c\\,|\\,b.$\n\nAlso, given that $p$ and $r$ are primes, we get\n\n${p}^{m}\\,|\\,{r}^{n}$ $\\,⟹\\,$ $p=r,$\n\nwhere $m$ and $n$ are positive integers.\n\nWith that in mind, we proceed as follows:\n\n- Since $p$ and $q$ are different primes, $\\text{gcd}(p,q)=1.$ Since $p\\,|\\,q{w}^{4},$ we must obtain that\n\n$$\np\\,|\\,{w}^{4}.\n$$\n\n- Since $p$ and $w$ are primes and $p\\,|\\,{w}^{4},$ we get\n\n$$\np=w.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
